    "result_text": "Green. I agreed with the finding and restructured accordingly.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe `/api/owners/` route is a REST-transport concern, so it no longer lives in the JPA domain entity:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 removed `getSelfLink()` entirely. The entity is back to carrying only genuine domain derivations.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** (the REST-boundary layer) \u2014 the `selfLink` is now computed during entity\u2192DTO translation:\n   - A `default String selfLink(Owner owner)` method is the single source of the path string, with the same `id == null` guard.\n   - `toOwnerDto` populates the field via `@Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", expression = \"java(selfLink(owner))\")`, keeping the auto-by-name wiring at the boundary instead of on the entity.\n\n3. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 the `Location` header now builds from `ownerMapper.selfLink(owner)`, so the header and the serialized `selfLink` field share one source and the duplicated literal is gone.\n\nThe `openapi.yml` schema addition was correct and stayed as-is. Full suite (`AcceptanceTest`, including `coreReturnsSelfLink`) passes.",
